# Best Train Backend - Project Rules

## Tech Stack

- Node.js, Express
- PostgreSQL (no ORM; raw SQL via SqlService)
- Globals: LogService, ResponseService, ConstantService, SqlService, Joi (from config/globals.js)

---

## Controller Conventions

When creating or modifying API controllers in `controllers/`, follow these rules:

### 1. Module Structure

- Flat export: `module.exports = { methodName: async (req, res) => { ... } }`
- No nested `API` wrapper
- JSDoc: API Endpoint, API Method, @param, @returns

### 2. Logging

```javascript
LogService.info("====================== API NAME API ==============================");
LogService.info("REQ QUERY : ", req.query);   // GET
LogService.info("REQ BODY : ", req.body);     // POST
```

### 3. Request Object

Build from `req.query` (GET) or `req.body` (POST). Pass raw values only—no defaults.

### 4. Validation (Joi Only)

- All validation in Joi schema
- All defaults in Joi (`.default(...)`), not in request object or destructuring
- `schema.validate(request, { abortEarly: false, stripUnknown: true })`
- Return 400 on error: `ResponseService.jsonResponse(res, ConstantService.responseCode.BAD_REQUEST, { message: error.message })`
- Extract validated values: `const { from, to, ... } = value`

### 5. Constants

Define constants after Joi validation, at the top of the handler logic.

### 6. Step Comments

Add numbered step comments for main logic blocks: `// Step 1:`, `// Step 2:`, etc. For nested logic: `// Step 6a:`, `// Step 6b:`.

### 7. Query Comments

Add a short comment above each SQL query explaining what it does and its parameters ($1, $2).

### 8. SQL

- Use parameterized queries ($1, $2, ...) only
- Never interpolate user input into SQL strings
- Use `SqlService.executeQuery(sql, params)`

### 9. Response

Success: `ResponseService.jsonResponse(res, ConstantService.responseCode.SUCCESS, { message: ..., data: { ... } })`

Error (catch): `ResponseService.json(res, ConstantService.responseCode.INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR, ConstantService.responseMessage.ERR_MSG_ISSUE_IN_...)`

### 10. Reference

- `controllers/trains/TrainController.js` – GET, complex queries, nearby search
- `controllers/stations/StationController.js` – POST, list with filters, pagination
